<h2>A Tour of Example Skills</h2>
<p>Now that the concepts are in place, let us look at real skill collections. When you are just getting started, opening up a few examples like these is recommended.</p>

<h3>Anthropic's built-in skills</h3>
<p>The built-in skills Anthropic made officially are published on GitHub. <strong>Copy a whole folder</strong> into Claude Code on your laptop and, on load, it reads only the <strong>YAML front matter</strong> of each <code>SKILL.md</code> first, loading the body when it is needed.</p>

<h3>A science agent skill collection (about 140 of them)</h3>
<p>There is also a collection that gathers skills for scientific research. It holds about <strong>140 science-related skills</strong>, enough for researchers in a field to say "the scripts we use a lot in our field are right here."</p>
<ul>
    <li>Bio-related skills such as <strong>Biopython</strong>, and a <strong>dataset download</strong> skill (down to where and how to get them).</li>
    <li><strong>Scientific Writing</strong> — it covers paper formats by conference and the rules for figures and tables (minimum resolution, no JPG but PNG, and so on), producing clean papers and PDFs.</li>
</ul>
<p>Thanks to the metadata you can <strong>load several skills at once</strong> and do <strong>interdisciplinary research</strong>. For example: "process this bio dataset with machine learning" → load bio → load data → train → on through writing and submitting the paper. Quantum and deep-learning hybrid processing is also possible to a degree.</p>

<h3>A Korea-focused skill collection</h3>
<p>There are also skill collections that are "by Koreans, for Koreans." They handle, right inside Claude Code (and the app), the things that used to be a nuisance every time in daily life.</p>
<ul>
    <li>SRT and KTX ticket booking, checking vacancies at recreational forests, KakaoMap</li>
    <li>Seoul subway arrival information, lost-and-found lookup, news and weather, Han River water levels</li>
    <li>Korean statute search, property registry extracts, HWP document viewing, parcel tracking, restaurants, and more</li>
</ul>

<div class="note">
    <span class="nh">The gap in between</span>
    The wide gap between the very <strong>scientific</strong> skills and the very <strong>everyday</strong> ones is one you can readily fill with skills for your own work.
</div>
